<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Napata</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Napata was an ancient city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> near the Fourth Cataract of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. It became a principal centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a> and before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>, and housed an important cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> that legitimised royal power. Kushite kings who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> as its Twenty-fifth Dynasty drew their authority from this religious centre.</p></div>
